# 🛡️ Identity & Access Management (IAM) Career Roadmap

## 1. Earn Microsoft SC-300 (Highest Priority)

**Certification:** Microsoft Certified: Identity and Access Administrator Associate (SC-300)

### Skills You'll Learn

- Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD)
- Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
- Conditional Access
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- Identity Governance
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)

> **Why It Matters:**  
> These are core IAM skills frequently listed in job descriptions for Identity and Access Management roles.

---

## 2. Learn Active Directory

Develop hands-on experience with:

- Creating user accounts
- Managing security groups
- Organizational Units (OUs)
- Group Policy basics
- Password policies
- Account lockouts
- User provisioning and deprovisioning

---

## 3. Learn PowerShell

You don't need to become a software developer—focus on automation tasks commonly performed by IAM administrators.

### Recommended Skills

- Create user accounts
- Disable user accounts
- Reset passwords
- Manage group memberships
- Write basic PowerShell scripts

> **Why It Matters:**  
> PowerShell is used daily by many Identity and Access Management teams.

---

## 4. Learn an IAM Platform

Gain experience with one or more of the following:

- Microsoft Entra ID ⭐ *(Recommended)*
- Okta
- SailPoint
- CyberArk (Privileged Access Management)

> **Recommendation:**  
> Start with Microsoft Entra ID, as Microsoft provides free learning paths and hands-on labs.

---

## 5. Build Hands-On Projects

Practical experience helps demonstrate your skills to employers.

### Suggested Projects

- Configure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
- Create Conditional Access policies
- Build user lifecycle workflows
- Configure RBAC roles
- Document your IAM environment
- Automate user creation with PowerShell

> Publish your projects on GitHub and include them on your résumé and LinkedIn profile.

---

# Target Job Titles

Consider applying for roles such as:

- IAM Analyst
- Identity Analyst
- Identity Administrator
- Access Management Analyst
- Active Directory Administrator
- Microsoft Entra ID Administrator
- Identity Governance Analyst
- Information Security Analyst (IAM)
- Junior IAM Engineer

> **Tip:**  
> Don't wait until you've earned the SC-300 certification. Your existing certifications already qualify you for many entry-level IT security and identity positions.

---

# Career Opportunities in Northern Virginia

Northern Virginia is one of the strongest job markets for Identity and Access Management professionals.

Many organizations rely on Microsoft identity technologies to secure enterprise environments. Candidates who are eligible for government contracting and can obtain a security clearance often have access to additional career opportunities.

---

# 90-Day Action Plan

## Weeks 1–4

- Study for the Microsoft SC-300 certification
- Complete Microsoft Learn training modules
- Practice in a free Microsoft 365 Developer environment

## Weeks 5–8

- Build hands-on IAM projects
- Configure Microsoft Entra ID
- Implement MFA
- Configure RBAC
- Practice PowerShell automation

## Weeks 9–12

- Earn the SC-300 certification
- Update your résumé and LinkedIn profile
- Apply to **10–15 IAM-related positions each week**
- Continue expanding your GitHub portfolio with IAM projects
